"""Source-authored bilingual manuscript. Review scope: depth-review-2026-10-20/REPORT.md."""
from model import p, ref, block, section

PART = dict(title=p('金錢服務經營者的系統及管控措施（一）：機構管治及策略', 'MSO systems and controls (i): institutional governance and strategy'),
intro=p('先理解機構承受甚麼風險，再把管理責任、資源、制度及覆核連起來。風險為本不代表可以免除法定責任。', 'Start with the risks faced by the institution, then connect management accountability, resources, controls and review. A risk-based approach does not waive statutory duties.'), sections=[
section('risk-based', '風險為本方法：資源與風險相稱', 'Risk-based approach: match resources to risk', [
    block('核心概念', 'Core concept', [
        ('風險為本方法（RBA），簡單來說，就是先弄清楚機構面對什麼洗錢或恐怖分子資金籌集風險，再按風險高低來管理及減低風險。資源應優先放在較高風險的範疇，而不是平均分配。', 'The risk-based approach (RBA), in plain terms, means first identifying, assessing and understanding the money-laundering and terrorist-financing risks the institution faces, and then managing and mitigating those risks with proportionate measures. Resources should be focused on higher-risk areas, not spread evenly.'),
        ('機構風險評估和客戶風險評估，是兩個層次，不要混為一談。機構評估針對的是整個業務，用來決定制度怎樣設計。客戶評估針對的是某一名客戶，或擬建立的關係，用來決定這次盡職審查和持續監察要做到什麼程度。例如：機構評估可能顯示匯款業務整體風險較高，因而加強整套監察制度；但對某一名低風險客戶，審查程度仍要按該客戶自己的評估來定，不能把兩層評估直接畫上等號。', 'Institutional risk assessment and customer risk assessment sit at two different levels, and should not be mixed up. Institutional assessment concerns the business as a whole, and shapes the control framework. Customer assessment concerns an individual customer, or a proposed relationship, and determines the extent of CDD and ongoing monitoring for that relationship. For example: an institutional assessment may show that remittance business is higher-risk overall, and the monitoring framework may be strengthened accordingly. The extent of CDD for a particular lower-risk customer still depends on that customer’s own assessment. The two layers are not the same exercise.'),
        ('評為低風險，可以支持相稱的簡化措施，但一般仍須完成四項盡職審查，以及持續監察。如果已經懷疑涉及洗錢或恐怖分子資金籌集，便不可以簡化制度。例如：即使某類產品被評為較低風險，仍不能略過識別及核實客戶等基本措施；一旦出現懷疑，簡化便必須停止。', 'A low-risk finding can support proportionate simplification, but the four CDD measures and ongoing monitoring generally still have to be completed. Systems cannot be simplified where money laundering or terrorist financing is suspected. For example: even if a product type is assessed as lower-risk, basic measures such as identifying and verifying the customer cannot be skipped. If suspicion arises, simplification must stop.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第2.1、2.13–2.16、3.3段', '¶2.1, 2.13–2.16, 3.3', 'allocate its resources more effectively'),
    ], kind='list'),
]),
section('institutional-assessment', '機構風險評估：因素、程序及更新', 'Institutional assessment: factors, process and updates', [
    block('評估涵蓋甚麼', 'Assessment scope', [
        ('機構風險評估首先要看客戶和國家這兩組因素。客戶方面：目標市場及客戶組別，以及高風險客戶的數目和比例。國家方面：客戶來自或所在的司法管轄區，以及機構本身的營運地點。', 'An institutional assessment starts with two groups of factors: customers and countries. On customers: the target markets and segments, and the number and proportion of high-risk customers. On countries: where customers come from or are located, and the jurisdictions in which the MSO itself operates.'),
        ('還要評估產品、服務及交易本身的風險。須考慮業務的性質、規模、多樣性和複雜程度；非經常交易、匿名性、交易量與客戶背景是否相符，以及科技可能被濫用的程度。', 'The risks in products, services and transactions must also be assessed. Consider the nature, scale, diversity and complexity of the business; occasional transactions; anonymity; whether volumes are consistent with customer profiles; and how far technology may be vulnerable to abuse.'),
        ('交付渠道也會改變風險高低。須考慮直接接觸客戶的程度、依賴第三方執行審查的程度、代理或對手機構網絡，以及付款鏈和結算系統的複雜性。例如：顧客多數親身到店，與大量透過海外代理、經過複雜付款鏈完成的匯款，風險圖像並不相同。', 'Delivery channels also affect the level of risk. Consider how directly the institution has contact with customers; how far it relies on third parties to carry out CDD; its agent or counterpart networks; and how complex the payment chains and settlement systems are. For example: a business in which most customers come into the shop in person does not have the same risk picture as one that relies heavily on overseas agents and complex payment chains.'),
        ('其他須納入評估的因素，包括風險管理資源的性質、規模及質素（包括具適當資格、並且可持續接受培訓的人員）、合規或監管發現，以及內部和外部審核結果。評估國家風險時，須考慮貪污、有組織罪行或恐怖分子資金籌集的普遍程度，執法水平及質素，監管制度及控制成效，以及實益擁有權的透明度。必須納入關長通知的較高風險，並及時評估擴散資金籌集風險。對應：document 09（把擴散融資納入機構風險評估）。', 'Other factors also belong in the assessment. They include the nature, scale and quality of risk-management resources, including qualified staff who receive continuing training, compliance or regulatory findings, and internal and external audits. Country risk considers the prevalence of corruption, organised crime or terrorist financing; the level and quality of law enforcement; the effectiveness of the regulatory regime and of controls; and the transparency of beneficial ownership. Include higher risks notified by the CCE and assess PF promptly under document 09.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第2.2–2.6段', '¶2.2–2.6', 'the number and proportion of customers identified as high risk'),
        ref('09', '正文第1–2頁', 'Main text pp.1–2', 'proliferation financing'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('完成及維持評估', 'Complete and maintain the assessment', [
        ('評估必須有紀錄，而且結果要獲高級管理層批准。須記錄識別及評估程序，結合內部和外部來源的定量及定性資料。先考慮全部相關因素，再判定整體風險及緩解措施。', 'The assessment must be documented, and the results must be approved by senior management. Document the identification and assessment process, using quantitative and qualitative information from internal and external sources. Consider all relevant factors before determining the overall risk and the mitigation.'),
        ('機構風險評估不是做一次便永久有效。至少每兩年評估一次，並在重大觸發事件發生時重做。觸發事件包括：出現嚴重制度違規、新增客戶組別、渠道或產品，或流程、目標客戶及業務對手出現重大改變。覆核結果同樣須記錄，並獲管理層批准。', 'An institutional assessment is not valid forever once it has been done. Assess at least every two years, and again when a material trigger occurs. Triggers include significant control breaches, new customer segments, channels or products, and significant changes to processes, target customers or counterparties. The review must be documented, and management approval obtained.'),
        ('評估資料要保存下來，並且在海關關長要求時能夠提供。須保存風險因素、資料來源，以及制度是否足夠及適當的評價，並設機制在關長要求時提供評估。規模較小、業務較簡單的機構，可以用較簡單的方法，但並不是因此免做評估。', 'The assessment materials must be kept, and must be capable of being provided if the CCE asks for them. Keep the risk factors, the information sources, and the evaluation of whether the controls are adequate and appropriate, and have a mechanism for providing the assessment to the CCE. A smaller, simpler business may use a simpler method. It is not exempt from doing an assessment.'),
        ('在本地成立、而且設有分行或附屬公司的機構，必須做集團層面的評估。可以參考或依賴集團或地區的評估，但該評估必須充分反映本地機構本身的風險。例如：集團總部的評估如果只談海外市場、沒有充分反映香港這間公司的客戶和渠道，便不能直接拿來代替本地評估。', 'A locally incorporated institution that has branches or subsidiaries must also assess risk on a group-wide basis. A group or regional assessment may be used only where it adequately reflects the local institution’s own risks. For example: a head-office assessment that deals only with overseas markets, and does not adequately reflect this Hong Kong company’s customers and channels, cannot be used as a substitute for the local assessment.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第2.3、2.5–2.10段', '¶2.3, 2.5–2.10', 'conduct its assessment every two years'),
    ], kind='list'),
]),
section('customer-assessment', '客戶風險評估：初評、定案及持續更新', 'Customer risk assessment: initial rating, finalisation and updates', [
    block('建立有依據的分級框架', 'An evidence-based rating framework', [
        ('每名客戶都要有風險分級，用來決定盡職審查和持續監察做到什麼程度。機構應建立客戶風險評估框架。在盡職審查初期先評估，以決定這次審查的程度；然後再統合審查結果、交易及背景資料作出定案，用以支持是否建立、繼續或終止關係的決定。', 'Every customer needs a risk rating, which is then used to decide how far CDD and ongoing monitoring should go. Maintain a framework that determines each customer’s money-laundering and terrorist-financing risk, and the intensity of CDD and monitoring. Assess at the initial CDD stage to set the extent of that CDD, then finalise the rating using the holistic CDD, transaction and background information, so as to support the decision whether to enter, continue or terminate the relationship.'),
        ('這套框架本身也要用風險為本方法，複雜程度須與業務性質及規模相稱，並以機構層面的風險評估結果為基礎。框架一般包含三組：(1) 客戶風險；(2) 國家風險；(3) 產品、服務、交易或交付渠道風險。這是整體評估，不是單用國籍或一個分數就可以代替分析。例如：不能只因為顧客持有某國護照，就把他一律列為高風險或低風險，而不看產品、渠道和實際交易模式。', 'The framework itself should use a risk-based approach. Its complexity should be proportionate to the nature and size of the business, and it should be based on the institutional risk assessment. It generally covers three groups: (1) customer risk; (2) country risk; and (3) product, service, transaction or delivery-channel risk. This is a holistic assessment, not something that can be replaced by nationality or by a single score. For example: a customer should not be rated high-risk or low-risk solely because of the passport he or she holds, without looking at the product, the channel and the actual transaction pattern.'),
        ('評估必須留有紀錄，證明兩件事：如何評估客戶風險；以及所用的盡職審查和持續監察程度，為何與該風險相稱。客戶風險會改變，應不時覆核及更新，尤其是在持續監察的過程中。下一組會說明2023年通函對「風險因素升高」的具體跟進要求。', 'The assessment and the relevant documents must be kept, so as to demonstrate two things: how the customer’s risk was assessed, and why the extent of CDD and ongoing monitoring is appropriate to that risk. Customer risk can change, so the rating should be reviewed and updated from time to time, particularly during ongoing monitoring. The next group sets out the specific 2023 circular requirements when a risk factor rises.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第2.13–2.16段', '¶2.13–2.16', 'finalise the customer risk assessment'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('2023年監管發現：風險因素上升後的跟進', '2023 supervisory findings: follow-up after a risk factor rises', [
        ('現有客戶的某一項風險因素如果被評為比以前更高，必須覆核是否要提高該客戶的整體洗錢或恐怖分子資金籌集風險級別。這是必須重新評估，並不是每一項因素一變，就自動把客戶列為最高風險。評級須有資料及推論紀錄，並向管理層及前線提供足夠指引，使同類因素得到一致處理。例如：顧客開始較常向一個較高風險地區匯款，機構必須重新檢視整體級別；但不能只因這一個因素，就自動把該客戶調到最高一級，而不記錄推論、也不看其他因素。', 'If any risk factor associated with an existing customer is assessed as posing a higher risk than before, the MSO must review whether that customer’s overall money-laundering or terrorist-financing risk level should be raised. Reassessment is mandatory. Automatically assigning the customer to the highest category is not the rule. Keep the supporting evidence and reasoning, and give management and front-line staff sufficient guidance so that similar factors are treated consistently. For example: if a customer starts remitting more often to a higher-risk jurisdiction, the overall rating must be reviewed. That single factor does not, by itself, automatically move the customer to the highest category, without recorded reasoning and without considering the other factors.'),
        ('通函有一個原文例子，用來說明資料不一致時要怎樣跟進，它不是一條「個人不得使用公司地址」的獨立禁令。例子是：客戶稱關係用於個人匯款，卻交出公司地址證明，並稱交易是支付貨款。這時必須追查不一致的資料，以建立準確的客戶檔案。若確定客戶就關係目的或性質有所誤導，或交易與已知背景或風險不符，應迅速查詢背景或目的，或補取盡職審查資料。如果得不到滿意解釋，可以構成懷疑；一旦識別出懷疑，便須向 JFIU 報告。例如：這是通函原本舉出的情況，複習時要記住跟進步驟，不要把它記成「個人一律不准用公司地址」。', 'The circular gives a source example of what to do when the information is inconsistent. It is not a separate rule forbidding an individual from using a company address. The source example is a customer who claims the relationship is for personal remittance, but provides a company address proof and describes the transaction as payment for goods. Follow up the inconsistencies so as to establish an accurate profile. If the customer has misled the MSO about the purpose or nature of the relationship, or if the transactions are inconsistent with the known background or risk, promptly examine the background or purpose, or obtain further CDD information. The absence of a satisfactory explanation may lead to suspicion. Identified suspicion requires a report to the JFIU. For example: this is the circular’s own illustration. Remember the follow-up steps; do not treat it as a separate prohibition on an individual using a company address.'),
    ], [
        ref('07', '正文第1項；附錄(1)，第1、3頁', 'Main finding 1; Appendix (1), pp.1, 3', 'should be elevated'),
    ], kind='list'),
]),
section('new-business', '新產品、渠道與科技：推出前評估', 'New products, channels and technology: assess before launch', [
    block('時間與責任', 'Timing and responsibility', [
        ('新產品、新渠道或新科技，必須在推出之前先做風險評估，不是先上線再補做。在發展新產品、新業務做法或新交付機制，以及為新的或現有的產品使用新的或發展中的科技之前，先識別及評估風險，並採取適當的管理和緩解措施。', 'New products, channels or technology must be risk-assessed before they are launched, not after they are already in use. Before launching a new product, business practice or delivery mechanism, or using new or developing technology for a new or existing product, identify and assess the risks and put appropriate management and mitigation measures in place.'),
        ('產品推出之後，如果業務出現重大改變，同樣會觸發更新機構風險評估。不能只在產品最初獲批時評估一次。例如：原本只做店舖兌換，後來新增一個網上匯款渠道，這類重大業務改變便應觸發再評估，而不是沿用推出前那一份舊評估。', 'After a product has been launched, a material change in the business also triggers an update of the institutional risk assessment. The assessment is not confined to the original product approval. For example: a firm that previously only did in-shop exchange and later adds an online remittance channel should treat that as a material business change that triggers reassessment, rather than continuing to rely on the pre-launch assessment.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第2.9、2.11–2.12段', '¶2.9, 2.11–2.12', 'prior to the launch of the new'),
    ], kind='list'),
]),
section('control-framework', '內控制度的組成與簡化條件', 'Control framework and conditions for simplification', [
    block('制度最低架構', 'Minimum framework', [
        ('內控制度必須與業務的性質、規模、複雜程度及風險相稱，而且有一個最低架構。至少包括合規管理安排、獨立審核、僱員甄選及持續培訓。制度應由高級管理層批准，並監察執行情況，在需要時加以改善。', 'Internal controls must be proportionate to the nature, size, complexity and risk of the business, and they have a minimum framework. That framework includes compliance management, independent audit, employee screening and continuing training. The MSO should have systems approved by senior management, should monitor how they are implemented, and should enhance them where necessary.'),
        ('機構必須採取一切合理措施，確保有適當保障，防止違反附表2第2部或第3部，並減低洗錢及恐怖分子資金籌集風險。這是法定責任，不是可有可無的良好做法。', 'The institution must take all reasonable measures to provide safeguards against contraventions of Parts 2 or 3 of Schedule 2, and to mitigate money-laundering and terrorist-financing risks. This is a legal duty, not an optional good practice.'),
        ('要簡化制度，必須同時符合三組條件，缺一不可；而且一旦有洗錢或恐怖分子資金籌集懷疑，便不得簡化。這三組是：(1) 繼續遵守附表2，並履行第2.2段的機構風險評估、第2.3段的評估程序，以及第3.2段的管理要求；(2) 已透過適當評估，識別出支持簡化的較低風險；(3) 簡化後的制度經高級管理層批准，並不時覆核。例如：不能只因為「我們是小店」，便在未做適當評估、也未經高級管理層批准的情況下，自行簡化審查制度。', 'A simplified control system is allowed only if three groups of conditions are all met. If money laundering or terrorist financing is suspected, simplification is not allowed. The three groups are: (1) continued compliance with Schedule 2, the institutional assessment under paragraph 2.2, the assessment process in paragraph 2.3, and the management requirements in paragraph 3.2; (2) lower risks identified through an appropriate assessment; and (3) senior-management approval, and periodic review, of the simplified systems. For example: being a small shop is not, by itself, a reason to simplify the CDD system without an appropriate assessment and without senior-management approval.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第3.1–3.4段', '¶3.1–3.4', 'an independent audit function'),
    ], kind='list'),
]),
section('roles', '高級管理層、合規主任與洗錢報告主任', 'Senior management, CO and MLRO', [
    block('三個角色的分工', 'Responsibilities of the three roles', [
        ('高級管理層、合規主任和洗錢報告主任，是三個不同角色，先要分清誰負責什麼。高級管理層應了解並有效管理機構風險，以及實施制度。它應任命管理層級的合規主任（Compliance Officer，CO）建立及維持制度，並任命高級職員為洗錢報告主任（Money Laundering Reporting Officer，MLRO），作為可疑交易報告的聯絡點。', 'Senior management, the Compliance Officer and the Money Laundering Reporting Officer are three different roles, and their responsibilities should be kept distinct. Senior management should understand and manage the institution’s risk, and implement the systems. It should appoint a management-level Compliance Officer (CO) to establish and maintain the controls, and a senior Money Laundering Reporting Officer (MLRO) as the focal point for suspicious-transaction reporting.'),
        ('合規主任是監督所有預防及偵察洗錢或恐怖分子資金籌集活動的中心點，並支援及指導高級管理層。四項主要職能是：(a) 制定及／或持續覆核制度，如屬在香港成立的金錢服務經營者，還包括任何集團制度，確保制度保持最新、符合法定及監管要求，並能有效管理風險；(b) 全面監察成效，有需要時加強管控或程序；(c) 向高級管理層傳達主要的打擊洗錢問題，包括在適用時的重大合規不足；(d) 確保培訓足夠、適當及有效。', 'The Compliance Officer is the focal point for overseeing all money-laundering and terrorist-financing prevention and detection activities, and for supporting and guiding senior management. The CO should (a) develop and/or continuously review the systems, including any group-wide systems for a Hong Kong-incorporated MSO, keeping them current, compliant and effective against risk; (b) oversee their effectiveness and implement enhanced controls or procedures where necessary; (c) communicate key AML/CFT issues, including significant compliance deficiencies where appropriate; and (d) ensure that training is adequate, appropriate and effective.'),
        ('洗錢報告主任專責處理可疑交易報告，角色與合規主任並不相同。MLRO 是可疑交易報告的中央聯絡點，也是與聯合財富情報組（JFIU）及執法機關的主要聯絡人，應積極參與識別及舉報。三項主要職能是：根據全部相關可得資料，覆核內部披露及例外報告，並決定是否向 JFIU 報告；保存所有內部覆核紀錄；以及指導員工如何避免通風報訊。', 'The Money Laundering Reporting Officer is the person who deals with suspicious transaction reports, and that role is not the same as the Compliance Officer’s. The MLRO is the central suspicious-reporting point and the main contact with the Joint Financial Intelligence Unit (JFIU) and law-enforcement agencies, and should play an active role in identification and reporting. The three principal functions are: reviewing internal disclosures and exception reports, using all available relevant information, and deciding whether to report to the JFIU; keeping all internal-review records; and guiding staff on how to avoid tipping off.'),
        ('視乎機構規模，合規主任與洗錢報告主任可以由同一人兼任；但兼任並不會免除其中任何一個角色的職責。例如：一間很小的店舖由同一名高級職員兼任兩個職位，這是可以的，但該人仍須同時履行 CO 的制度監督職責，以及 MLRO 的舉報及覆核職責。', 'Depending on the size of the institution, the same person may be both CO and MLRO. Holding both posts does not remove either set of responsibilities. For example: a very small shop may appoint the same senior staff member to both roles. That is permissible, but that person must still perform the CO’s system-oversight duties and the MLRO’s reporting and review duties.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第3.5–3.10段及註9', '¶3.5–3.10; footnotes 9', 'functions of CO and MLRO may be performed by the same'),
    ], kind='comparison'),
    block('職位履職條件', 'Conditions enabling the roles', [
        ('高級管理層應在切實可行範圍內，確保合規主任和洗錢報告主任具備指引第3.8段的八項條件。先記前四項：(a) 具備適當資格及充足的打擊洗錢知識；(b) 在機構規模容許下，獨立於所有營運及業務職能；(c) 通常在香港工作；(d) 有足夠資歷及權限。', 'As far as practicable, senior management should ensure that the CO and the MLRO meet the eight conditions in Guideline paragraph 3.8. The first four are: (a) appropriate qualifications and sufficient AML/CFT knowledge; (b) independence from all operational and business functions, subject to the MSO’s size; (c) normally based in Hong Kong; and (d) sufficient seniority and authority.'),
        ('其餘四項條件是：(e) 可定期接觸高級管理層，並在需要時直接接觸；(f) 充分熟悉機構的法定及監管規定，以及業務所產生的風險；(g) 能及時取得所有可得資料，包括內部盡職審查紀錄及外部的海關通函；(h) 有充足資源、人員及缺勤時的替代安排。副手的具體措辭，見本節下文。', 'The remaining four conditions are: (e) regular contact with senior management, and direct access to them when needed; (f) full familiarity with the MSO’s statutory and regulatory requirements and with the risks of the business; (g) timely access to all available information, including internal CDD records and external Customs circulars; and (h) sufficient resources, staff and cover for absences. The specific wording about a deputy is set out later in this section.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第3.6、3.8段', '¶3.6, 3.8', 'normally based in Hong Kong'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('任職形式', 'Appointment basis', [
        ('合規主任及洗錢報告主任必須是僱員，但由獨資經營者、合夥人、董事或最終擁有人擔任者除外。不能只借用外部顧問的名銜，而沒有實際職權與投入。例如：請一間顧問公司掛名為「合規主任」，但該人不是僱員，也不是東主、合夥、董事或最終擁有人，而且日常並無實權，這樣並不符合這項任職要求。', 'The CO and the MLRO must be employees, unless the role is held by the proprietor, a partner, a director or an ultimate owner. An external adviser’s title, on its own, does not provide actual authority or engagement. For example: naming a consultant as “Compliance Officer”, where that person is not an employee and is not the proprietor, a partner, a director or an ultimate owner, and has no real day-to-day authority, does not meet this appointment requirement.'),
    ], [
        ref('05', '第4.15(a)段', '¶4.15(a)', 'employee under the definition'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('管理資料的接收人及替補安排', 'Management-information recipients and deputy cover', [
        ('給高級管理層看的管理資料，必須讓人及時看懂、內容完整而且準確。這些資料應及時、完整、易明及準確地，向董事會或獲轉授的委員會（如適用）以及高級管理層傳達。應在切實可行範圍內提供足夠資源及缺席時的替補安排；如切實可行，應安排替代或代理的合規主任及洗錢報告主任，而其應具有相同地位。', 'Management information for senior management has to arrive in time, and it has to be complete, clear and accurate. Timely, complete, understandable and accurate management information should go to the board or a delegated committee where applicable, and to senior management. As far as practicable, sufficient resources and cover for absences should be provided. An alternate or deputy CO and MLRO should, where practicable, have the same status.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第3.6、3.8(h)段', '¶3.6, 3.8(h)', 'an alternate or deputy CO and MLRO'),
    ], kind='list'),
]),
section('group-controls', '海外分行及附屬公司：集團制度', 'Overseas branches and subsidiaries: group controls', [
    block('適用範圍與較高標準', 'Scope and higher standards', [
        ('在香港成立的機構，如果海外分行或附屬公司從事與條例所界定金融機構相同的業務，便要在適用範圍內實施集團打擊洗錢制度。這包括與附表2相若的盡職審查及備存紀錄程序。', 'Group-wide AML controls apply where a Hong Kong-incorporated institution has overseas branches or subsidiaries carrying on the same business as an AMLO financial institution. A Hong Kong-incorporated MSO applies group-wide controls to overseas branches/subsidiaries carrying on the same business as an AMLO financial institution, where relevant, including comparable CDD and record-keeping procedures.'),
        ('在當地法律容許的範圍內，須採用香港與所在地兩套規定之中較高的標準。如果當地法律不容許採用較高標準，須通知海關關長，並採取額外措施，有效減低由此產生的風險。例如：所在地法律的盡職審查要求較香港寬鬆，在當地法律容許時，仍應採用較高的香港標準，而不是自動跟隨當地的較低要求。', 'To the extent the host country’s law permits, the higher of the Hong Kong requirements and the host requirements must be applied. If host law prevents that, the CCE must be informed, and additional measures must be taken that effectively mitigate the resulting risks. For example: if the host country’s CDD requirements are less demanding than Hong Kong’s, the higher Hong Kong standard should still be applied where host law allows, rather than automatically following the lower local requirement.'),
        ('集團內可以為盡職審查及風險管理而分享資料，並在需要時向集團合規、審核及打擊洗錢職能，提供客戶、戶口和交易資料。但必須符合法律，以及保密、用途限制、避免通風報訊等保障。不是集團內部便可以任意傳閱客戶資料。', 'Information may be shared within the group for CDD and risk management and, where necessary, customer, account and transaction information may be provided to group compliance, audit and AML functions. This remains subject to the law, and to safeguards for confidentiality, permitted use and the prevention of tipping off. Group membership is not a licence to circulate customer information freely.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第3.15–3.19段', '¶3.15–3.19', 'apply the higher of the two sets of requirements'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('遷冊來港實體', 'Re-domiciled entities', [
        ('遷冊來港的實體，其海外分行或附屬公司同樣受這套法定要求約束，不能因為較早的指引只提到「香港成立」的機構，便忽略這個範圍。綜合條例附表2第22條，亦涵蓋遷冊來港實體的海外分行及附屬公司要求。對應：Schedule 2 section 22。', 'A re-domiciled entity’s overseas branches or subsidiaries are also within this statutory duty. An earlier Guideline that mentions only Hong Kong-incorporated institutions does not remove that scope. Schedule 2 section 22 in the consolidated Ordinance also covers re-domiciled entities’ overseas branches/subsidiaries. The older Guideline’s reference to Hong Kong incorporation does not remove that statutory scope.'),
    ], [
        ref('04', '附表2第22條', 'Schedule 2 s.22', 'a re-domiciled entity'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('異常交易分析與集團雙向分享', 'Unusual-transaction analysis and two-way group sharing', [
        ('在法律容許，以及保密、用途和防止通風報訊的保障下，集團分享應包括已經完成的異常交易或活動分析。可以包括可疑交易報告、其底層資料，或已經呈報的事實，但並非一律強制分享每一份可疑交易報告。集團職能也應在與風險管理相關、而且適當時，向分行或附屬公司回傳資料。例如：集團合規部門完成一宗異常匯款分析後，可在保障範圍內把分析結果與相關海外分行分享，並在適當時把有用的風險資料回傳給該分行；但不表示每一份已向 JFIU 提交的報告都必須在集團內傳閱。', 'Subject to the law, and to safeguards on confidentiality, use and tipping off, group sharing should include analysis of unusual transactions or activities, if that analysis has been done. It could include a suspicious transaction report, the underlying information, or the fact that a report has been made. It is not a rule that every STR must be shared. Group functions should also pass relevant and appropriate risk-management information back to branches or subsidiaries. For example: after group compliance has analysed an unusual remittance, the analysis may, within those safeguards, be shared with the relevant overseas branch, and useful risk information may be passed back to that branch where appropriate. That does not mean every report already filed with the JFIU must be circulated around the group.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第3.17段及註11', '¶3.17; footnotes 11', 'This should include information and analysis of transactions or activities which appear unusual'),
    ], kind='list'),
]),
section('business-plan', '業務計劃：把營運模式交代完整', 'Business plan: explain the complete operating model', [
    block('提交內容', 'Required content', [
        ('業務計劃是讓金錢服務監理科了解擬議業務和運作模式的文件，資料不足可以延誤或妨礙牌照申請。計劃須同時處理營運與合規目標，並且顯示有足夠資源去執行。', 'The business plan is the document that lets the Money Service Supervision Bureau understand the proposed business and how it will operate. Missing information may delay or hinder a licence application. The plan must address both operational and compliance objectives, and must show that there are resources to carry them out.'),
        ('機構背景須交代：公司或業務名稱、網站、標誌及商標；歷史、資本來源和集團關係；高級管理人員的國籍、經驗、資格及教育；決策地點，以及境內外的後勤辦事處。', 'The institutional background must cover: the company or business names, website, logo and trademark; the history, sources of capital and group links; the nationality, experience, qualifications and education of senior executives; and where decisions are made, together with any local or overseas back offices.'),
        ('客戶及交易部分須交代：預期客戶的所在地、國籍及接觸方式；在香港的業務，以及申請牌照的原因；由落單、處理、資金流、合規，以至會計和備存紀錄的完整流程。', 'The customers and transactions part must cover: where expected customers are located, their nationality and how they will be contacted; the Hong Kong operations and the reasons for seeking a licence; and the entire process, from instructions and processing through fund flows, compliance, accounting and record-keeping.'),
        ('產品及渠道部分須交代：產品和服務與推出時間、各地代理或海外經營者及服務協議，以及對手不履約時如何保護客戶資金。須交代銀行戶口號碼及擁有人，不可使用第三方銀行戶口；如果不用銀行戶口，則須說明如何經營。例如：不能把客戶資金放進一名員工或親友的私人銀行戶口來周轉，計劃裡必須寫明業務戶口及其擁有人。', 'The products and channels part must cover: the services and their launch dates; overseas agents or operators and the service agreements; and how customer funds will be protected if a counterparty fails to perform. Identify the business bank accounts and their owners. Third-party bank accounts are not allowed. If no bank account is needed, explain how the business will operate. For example: customer funds must not be run through an employee’s or a relative’s personal bank account. The plan must identify the business accounts and their owners.'),
        ('財務及架構部分須交代：未來兩年各產品的預期利潤率及營業額、日常營運資本、本地及海外集團架構圖、共用處所的其他業務的性質及關係，以及本地管理層和僱員的職責、人數、全職或兼職身分與匯報線。', 'The finance and structure part must cover: expected margins and turnover by product for the next two years; working capital; local and international group charts; the nature of any other businesses sharing the premises and their relationships; and the numbers, duties, full-time or part-time status and reporting lines of local management and staff.'),
        ('其他安排還須交代：外判服務、自動化或篩查系統、作為代理或主事人的角色、第三方付款平台、實體現金運送，以及其他監管機構的監管情況。計劃還須書面確認：申請資料如有變更，會在一個月內通知關長。', 'Other arrangements still have to be covered: outsourcing; automated or screening systems; whether the firm acts as agent or as principal; third-party payment platforms; physical movements of cash; and supervision by any other regulator. The plan must also confirm in writing that changes to the licensing particulars will be notified to the CCE within one month.'),
    ], [
        ref('20', '第1–17項及引言', 'Introduction and items 1–17', 'No third party bank account is allowed'),
    ], kind='list'),
]),
section('policy', '打擊洗錢政策：與本身業務及風險連接', 'AML/CFT policy: connect controls to the actual business', [
    block('政策須可以實際執行', 'An operational policy', [
        ('打擊洗錢政策必須先根據自身風險來寫，不能直接套用一份與本身業務不符的範本。應先做自身風險評估，再按產品、渠道、架構、客戶及地理風險，制定政策、程序和管控措施。提交指引上的清單並不是盡列的。', 'An AML/CFT policy has to be written from the institution’s own risks. A generic template that does not fit the actual business is not enough. Assess the MSO’s own risks first, then design the policies, procedures and controls for its products, channels, structure, customers and geographical risks. The submission checklist is not exhaustive.'),
        ('政策須交代法律框架、合規主任和洗錢報告主任及匯報線、盡職審查的觸發門檻與相連交易、客戶風險評估、簡化審查及加強審查、政治人物、非親身渠道、高風險國家、財富及資金來源，以及審查失敗時如何處理。', 'The policy must explain the legal framework; the CO, the MLRO and the reporting lines; CDD thresholds and linked transactions; customer risk assessment; simplified and enhanced due diligence; PEPs; non-face-to-face channels; higher-risk countries; sources of wealth and of funds; and what happens if CDD cannot be completed.'),
        ('還要說明持續的客戶及交易監察、紀錄保存與檢索、產品、貨幣、目標客戶、分別列明匯入及匯出的目標司法管轄區和收入模式、付款及結算流程、代理或海外分支的監察，以及制裁與政治人物篩查。渠道說明還須包括面對面及非面對面交易所佔的百分比。', 'It must also describe ongoing customer and transaction monitoring; record retention and retrieval; products, currencies, target customers, and, separately for inward and outward business, the target jurisdictions and revenue; payment and settlement flows; supervision of overseas branches or agents; and sanctions and PEP screening. The description of channels must include the percentages of face-to-face and non-face-to-face transactions.'),
        ('政策還須列出合規管理、可疑交易辨識及舉報、獨立審核、按職責提供培訓及成效監察、其他內控，以及配合海關或執法機構的安排。可以附上開戶、風險評估及內部報告表格，展示這些安排如何實際落實。', 'The policy must also set out compliance management; the detection and reporting of suspicious transactions; independent audit; role-based training and monitoring of its effectiveness; other internal controls; and arrangements for cooperating with Customs or law-enforcement agencies. Onboarding, risk-assessment and internal-report forms may be attached to show how the arrangements are put into practice.'),
        ('政策指引裡提到「例如一天內檢索紀錄」，只是用來說明應具備怎樣的檢索能力，並不是把所有法定期限都改成一天。實際法律，以及個別命令所規定的期限，仍須分開遵守。例如：關長如果命令你在某個指定期限內交出紀錄，須遵守該命令的期限；不能因為指引舉過「一天內檢索」的例子，就把所有法定期限一律改成一天，或一律當成只要一天便足夠。', 'Where the policy guide gives the example of retrieving records within one day, that is only an illustration of retrieval capability. It does not replace every legal deadline with a one-day rule. The relevant law, and the time limits in any individual order, must still be applied separately. For example: if the CCE orders records to be produced within a specified period, that order’s deadline must be met. The guide’s “one-day retrieval” illustration does not turn every legal time limit into one day, and it does not mean that one day is always enough.'),
    ], [
        ref('21', '引言、第1–19項', 'Introduction; items 1–19', 'say one day'),
    ], kind='list'),
]),
])
